1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
CARDIO EM operating demonstration

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,900
Precision ECG analysis once found only in hospitals,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,500
now light enough for anywhere.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,300
On the ward, in a moving ambulance,

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,100
and out at remote consultations.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:28,900
The system consists of a sensor module, a cradle and an electrode holder.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,500
The limb-lead cable and electrode patch are optional.

8
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,700
Disposable electrodes are prepared separately.

9
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,900
The sensor module charges with the charging cable.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,700
First, check each component.

11
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:56,100
Seat the sensor module on the cradle to charge it.

12
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:03,100
Orange means charging; green means charging is complete.

13
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:11,600
Install the CARDIO PRO app and turn Bluetooth on.

14
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:17,600
Connect disposable electrodes to the limb-lead cable.

15
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:24,400
Peel the liner back slightly and attach the electrode holder.

16
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:29,600
Clip the limb-lead cable into the holder.

17
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:36,000
The sensor module goes on once the electrodes are secure on the chest.

18
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:42,600
Electrodes must touch bare skin, not clothing.

19
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:46,800
Place the electrode patch on the chest.

20
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:54,600
Attach limb electrodes RA, LA, RL and LL at their positions.

21
00:01:54,700 --> 00:02:00,200
Once everything is secure, attach the sensor module.

22
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:08,700
Log in to the app. First time? Create an account.

23
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:14,500
Tap Bluetooth Connect on the home screen.

24
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:22,700
When CARDIO EM appears, tap the Bluetooth button to connect.

25
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:29,900
Once connected, press Play to open the measurement screen.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,400
Check electrode status at the top right. Red means unstable contact.

27
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:46,900
If contact is poor, press again to secure; for dry skin, apply lotion or wipe it first.

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,900
When all turn green, press Play to start measuring.

29
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:02,900
Live waveforms and heart rate appear, and filters can be set.

30
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:10,300
Tap Stop to end the measurement and save the record.

31
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:18,100
Find saved records under Import Data on the home screen.

32
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:24,700
Filter and sort to find a record, then tap it to open the waveform.

33
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:32,500
Beat classification separates normal from abnormal beats.

34
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:39,300
Atrial fibrillation or flutter appears under Rhythm classification.

35
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:45,100
The trend graph shows heart-rate changes over time.

36
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:53,600
Save a region of interest as a 10-second ECG strip, 5 s either side.

37
00:03:53,700 --> 00:04:00,400
On the move, the steps are the same. Attach the sensor module,

38
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:07,000
check electrode status on the tablet and start measuring.

39
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:11,800
Watch live waveforms and heart rate,

40
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:17,600
then save the record and share it with the hospital.

41
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:25,600
Tap the PDF icon to see the waveform on ECG paper.

42
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:33,600
PR, QRS, QT and QTc values are shown with it.

43
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:40,600
Adjust the gain, then save as PDF or share.

44
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:48,800
After use, detach the sensor module and store it on the cradle or holder.

45
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:55,800
Precision ECG analysis once found only in hospitals, now light enough for anywhere.
